The code first reads the input file and stores all the data points in an array. Then it applies a series of mathematical operations to each data point based on the rules specified in the configuration file. Finally, it writes the processed data to the output file.

You can use this program as follows:
```
./process_data <input_file> <config_file> <output_file>
```
where `<input_file>` is the path to the input file, `<config_file>` is the path to the configuration file, and `<output_file>` is the path to the output file. For example:
```
./process_data data/example.txt config/example.conf data/example_processed.txt
```']

