The implementation uses a `Map` to store the configurations of each service and a `List` to track the active services. It also includes a `Service` class that encapsulates the logic for starting and stopping a service. The `startService()` method will try to start a service with a specified name, respecting the maximum restart attempts and exponential backoff for retries. Similarly, the `stopService()` method will try to stop a service with a specified name, respecting the maximum restart attempts and exponential backoff for retries.

