The function `loadInitialContextData()` takes a filename as input and reads the header line of the CSV file to get the number of columns in the file. It then allocates memory for an array of `UEContext` structures with the same number of columns, and reads the rows of the CSV file to populate the array. If there are any parsing errors or memory allocation failures, it handles them gracefully.

