This function first locks the mutex, and then frees any memory that was allocated for the `crc_indications` array. It also sets the count to zero, indicating that there are no more CRC indications in the list. Finally, it unlocks the mutex before returning.

## Realloc Code

The realloc code is responsible for handling out-of-memory errors that may occur when trying to allocate memory using `malloc()`. If a reallocation fails, this function will attempt to reduce the size of the allocation in order to make it more likely that the program will be able to continue running.

Here is an example of realloc code for the `crc_indications` data structure:
