    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
    return new_list;
}
```
This function first locks the mutex, and then attempts to reallocate the `crc_indications` array using `realloc()`. If this fails, it will attempt to reduce the size of the allocation by half in order to make it more likely that the program will be able to continue running. Finally, it unlocks the mutex before returning the new list.

