The code also uses logging mechanisms for error handling and debugging purposes. Whenever there is an error during memory allocation or file reading, the function logs an error message and exits. The `handleErrors` function is called whenever there is an error, which logs the error message and line number where the error occurred.

The code also uses caching mechanisms to minimize redundant decompression operations and optimize memory usage. Whenever a compressed file is read, it is cached in memory for future use. This reduces the amount of time spent on decompression and improves performance.

In terms of concurrency, the function uses a mutex to synchronize access to the shared data structure `items`. This ensures that concurrent access to the items array does not result in race conditions or deadlocks.']

