The function `enqueue` adds an item to the queue, blocking until there is enough space in the queue. The function `dequeue` removes an item from the front of the queue, blocking until there are items in the queue.

To manage dynamic pool allocation and deallocation efficiently, we use a mutex to synchronize access to the queue. We also use a condition variable to signal between threads when there is enough space in the queue or when it is empty.

To ensure that no two items within the pool share the same `TASK_ID`, we generate unique IDs for each item by incrementing a counter.

