### NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU data structure

The `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU` data structure contains the CRC indication information. It has the following members:

* `sfn_s_subframe`: The serial number of the sub-frame in which the CRC information was received. This is a 12-bit field that represents a combination of the system frame number (SFN) and the sub-frame number (S).
* `crc_info`: An array of `NFAPI_CRC_INFO` structures, each representing one CRC information element. The length of this array is defined by the `num_crc_infos` field.

The `NFAPI_CRC_INFO` data structure contains the following members:

* `rnti`: The RNTI (Reliable Non-Time Critical Identifier) of the PDSCH transmission for which the CRC information is reported. This is a 16-bit field that represents the RNTI value.
* `crc_data`: A byte array representing the actual CRC data received. The length of this array is defined by the `crc_length` field.

