The cache of recently accessed cell IDs is used to minimize the impact of network latency on performance by reusing the same cell ID values whenever possible. The cache size is limited to `MAX_CELLS` to prevent excessive memory allocation and to maintain responsiveness to user requests even under degraded conditions.

