3. Implement the `HttpClient` interface to handle both synchronous and asynchronous HTTP requests using OkHttp:
```java
public class HttpClient implements HttpClientInterface {
    private final OkHttpClient client = new OkHttpClient();

    @Override
    public ResponseElement getResponse(String url) throws IOException {
        Request request = new Request.Builder()
                .url(url)
                .build();
        Response response = client.newCall(request).execute();
        return new ResponseElement(response.code(), response.headers().toMultimap(), response.body().string());
    }

    @Override
    public void getResponseAsync(String url, Consumer<ResponseElement> callback) {
        Request request = new Request.Builder()
                .url(url)
                .build();
        client.newCall(request).enqueue(new Callback() {
            @Override
            public void onResponse(Call call, Response response) throws IOException {
                callback.accept(new ResponseElement(response.code(), response.headers().toMultimap(), response.body().string()));
            }

            @Override
            public void onFailure(Call call, Throwable t) {
                callback.accept(null);
            }
        });
    }
}
```
