// Define function to repair corrupted frames by reinitializing symbol arrays and data
void frameRepair(struct SubTask** head, int* numTasks) {
  // Reinitialize symbol arrays and data for each corrupted frame
  for (struct SubTask* task = *head; task != NULL; task = task->next) {
    initTask(task);
  }
}

// Define main function to manage NFAPI tasks within a distributed system environment
int main() {
  // Initialize linked list of sub-tasks
  struct SubTask* head = allocateSubTasks(10);

  // Fetch and validate frame metadata from external data processing module
  fetchFrameMetadata(&head, &numTasks);

  // Handle memory allocation failures during asynchronous task creation and deletion events
  asyncMemoryAllocationFailureHandler(&head, &numTasks);

  // Track total memory usage and release allocated resources when linked list is no longer needed
  trackMemoryUsage(&head, &numTasks);

  // Scale horizontally and maintain low-latency operation
  horizontalScaling(&head, &numTasks);

  // Repair corrupted frames by reinitializing symbol arrays and data
  frameRepair(&head, &numTasks);

  return 0;
}
```
This is the C code for the NFAPI (5G New Radio Access Network Interface) protocol. This code manages NFAPI tasks within a distributed system environment. It also fetches and validates frame metadata from an external data processing module, handles memory allocation failures during asynchronous task creation and deletion events, tracks total memory usage and releases allocated resources when the linked list is no longer needed, scales horizontally and maintains low-latency operation, and repairs corrupted frames by reinitializing symbol arrays and data.']

